# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Added 2026-08-31, after commit 6446235 ("catchup") rewrote every line of
# i1_wakeup_music.py as CRLF. The content was byte-identical -- verified by
# comparing both blobs with \r stripped -- but the diff read as 1445
# insertions and 1445 deletions. That makes review impossible, and would
# have concealed a real change had one been mixed in. Backlog tickets
# T-20..T-29 cite line numbers in that file, so a silent content change
# there is not hypothetical.
#
# text=auto lets git detect which files are text; eol=lf pins the
# working-tree ending so an editor on another machine cannot reintroduce
# CRLF and produce the same unreviewable diff again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats are never normalised. These carry incidental \r\n byte
# pairs that a text pass would corrupt.
*.parquet binary
*.pyc     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
